# Build-context pruning. Ported from windows-ai-sandbox (work/0001 A3).
#
# The Dockerfile COPYs exactly four paths, all under sandbox_templates/ (.zshrc,
# .p10k.zsh, claude/hooks/deny-destructive.sh, and the wheels/ DIRECTORY).
# Everything else in this repo is context that gets tarred and shipped to the
# Colima VM on every build for nothing — 312M sent to deliver ~180K.
#
# sandbox_templates/wheels/ is deliberately NOT pruned here even though its .whl
# is gitignored: .dockerignore does not inherit .gitignore (point 1 below), and
# the wheel is a build INPUT. Pruning it would make the myclickup layer silently
# take its no-wheel branch on a machine that has the payload — a green build that
# ships an image without the tool.
#
# Two things to know before editing:
#   1. .dockerignore does NOT inherit .gitignore. Anything that must stay out
#      of a build layer has to be repeated here even if git already ignores it.
#   2. A bare `*.md` matches root-level files ONLY — `*` does not cross `/`.
#      Nested markdown needs its directory listed (docs/, work/ below).
#
# This is a denylist, so its failure mode is silent under-pruning. If you add a
# large directory to the repo, add it here too. And if a future COPY needs a
# path listed below, remove that line rather than working around it — a missing
# COPY source fails the build loudly, which is the good outcome.

# --- VCS and repo metadata ---
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore

# --- Prose and assets: nothing is COPYed from any of these ---
*.md
docs/
work/
images/

# --- Editor / OS / agent-session state ---
.vscode/
.claude/
**/.DS_Store

# --- Secrets: must never enter a build layer, even an unreferenced one ---
.env
.env.*
**/secrets.env

# --- The dashboard's venv: 307M of the 312M context, i.e. nearly all of it ---
dashboard/.venv

# --- Runtime-only inputs. Compose and the daemon read these from the HOST
#     path at container start (bind mounts, and security_opt for seccomp),
#     never from the build context, so pruning them cannot affect the sandbox.
proxy/
seccomp.json
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml

# --- Host-side tooling: runs on the Mac or via docker exec, never in a layer ---
scripts/

# --- Generated / external state that can appear here but never builds ---
profiles/
temp_audit_package/
